            "notes": "If you did not get [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505) in Round 4 definetly get it in Round 5. If you want your build to focus more on debuffing the enemies, I suggest you go with [Liquid Nitrogen](item_a8d99526-05a3-4405-babb-b025479b1b98) next for the Slow effect, though [Catalytic Crystal](item_3e3f4f77-cdf8-4dda-a5b0-2fb9390aefc4) or [Lum\u00e9riCo Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) work also - especially if you need survivability without sacrificing [Ability Power](stat_ability_power).\nAs for the Power, if your team is doing fine on Survivability and Healing, I would go for [Cosmic Coolant](item_5584169d-94af-4efa-955c-263353a75553) to allow you to use your Torpedos more often. If the healing output is fine but the enemy team has a lot of Burst Damage, I suggest going for [Hyper Healer](item_108336b3-54d2-4d69-8ea4-c2da5affb7ca) as it works nicely with our [Ability Power](stat_ability_power) focused build already. If the healing output is severely lacking, definitetly go with [Medicinal Missiles](item_30eeab6c-4a1e-4a16-b9dd-e83d633caa40) as you will function as a sort of mini-Ana for your team, able to boost all healing for 3s.",
